{
  "slug": "erdos-73-oq-02",
  "title": "Improved Erdős–Pósa Bounds for Odd Cycles",
  "phase": "OBSERVE",
  "status": "active",
  "tier": "C",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\exists\\, C > 0 \\;\\; \\forall\\, G,\\, k:\\quad \\nu_{\\mathrm{odd}}(G) \\le k \\;\\Longrightarrow\\; \\tau_{\\mathrm{odd}}(G) \\le C\\, k \\log k",
    "plain": "A graph is bipartite exactly when it has no odd cycle. Two measures of non-bipartiteness are the odd-cycle packing number (max vertex-disjoint odd cycles) and the odd-cycle transversal number (fewest vertices whose deletion destroys all odd cycles). The Erdős–Pósa property says the transversal is bounded by a function of the packing number; the goal is to formalize the packing–transversal duality and sharpen the best known bounding function f(k) = O(k log k).",
    "whyMatters": [
      "The packing–transversal gap for odd cycles is the engine behind Reed's almost-bipartite theorem for Erdős Problem #73, so improving it improves the bipartite deficiency bound.",
      "Odd-cycle Erdős–Pósa bounds control constants in fixed-parameter algorithms for Odd Cycle Transversal and Maximum Bipartite Subgraph.",
      "Odd cycles are the canonical example separating cases where the Erdős–Pósa property holds (planar / highly connected) from where it fails entirely."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "Erdős–Pósa theorem for cycles (Erdős & Pósa 1965): O(k log k) transversal for arbitrary cycles, order tight.",
      "Reed's theorem / Erdős #73 (Reed 1999): k-independence condition implies bipartite plus O_k(1) vertices, f(k) ≤ 2^k.",
      "Odd Erdős–Pósa in planar / highly connected graphs (Reed 1999; Rautenbach–Reed 2001; Thomassen 2001): f(k) = O(k log k)."
    ],
    "open": [
      "Optimal growth rate of f(k) where odd-cycle Erdős–Pósa holds: is O(k log k) tight or does O(k) suffice?",
      "Whether the Erdős #73 deficiency bound can be reduced from exponential 2^k toward polynomial/linear via improved transversal constants."
    ],
    "goal": "Formalize on the erdos-73 framework the odd-cycle packing–transversal chain: the trivial inequality ν_odd ≤ τ_odd, the identity τ_odd(G) = bipartiteDeficiency G, and an axiomatized Erdős–Pósa bound τ_odd(G) ≤ f(ν_odd(G)) with O(k log k) growth."
  },
